{
  "season": 1,
  "week": 18,
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "injury-report-s1-w18",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "tessa-wren",
      "title": "Injury Report: 88 Special, Exploud and Gabite miss the playoff opening",
      "dek": "New losses for Sunyshore, Cinnabar and Olivine; Eterna loses another target, and Mt. Silver’s bye begins with a long availability list.",
      "teams": [],
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Sunyshore opens the playoffs without 88 Special, whose new reported absence is sixteen weeks. The receiver finished the regular season with ten receiving touchdowns, including two in the penultimate game. Cinnabar has lost Exploud for six weeks, Olivine has lost Gabite for eight, and Eterna has a new two-week absence for Dewgong. Those changes arrive before home-and-away assignments already fixed by the final standings."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Sunyshore and Cinnabar lose productive targets"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "88 Special caught two passes for twenty-six yards in the 23–3 win at Veilstone. His season total of 526 receiving yards and ten touchdowns makes the loss substantial before Hearthome visits. Fera LaGatr remains an established option after seventy-three catches for 766 yards, while MF STOMP caught seven passes for seventy-six in the finale. Those are observed contributions; the playoff distribution has not been announced."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Cinnabar’s Exploud finished with fifty-seven catches, 657 yards and four receiving touchdowns. His six-week absence removes a productive tight end before the Blackthorn rematch. Arcanine remains out one reported week; the player’s recorded defensive work includes eight sacks, so treating the listed halfback position as the whole injury impact would miss an important job. Blackthorn also has Exploud out one week and Sawsbuck out four."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Olivine and Eterna face immediate adjustments"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Olivine qualified with a shutout at Azalea and now travels to Saffron with Gabite out eight weeks. Gabite accumulated 702 rushing yards. Stantler and Gogoat remain out four weeks apiece, and Beedrill has a new twelve-week absence. The Ironclads must assemble enough offense against a Saffron defense that allowed 138 points; the Psi Corps have no current positive-week injury entry."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Eterna’s new two-week absence for Dewgong removes a receiver with 375 season yards. Tatsugiri remains out six weeks and Stantler one. Slowking completed the finale at quarterback as the Thorns beat Snowpoint 9–3; the prior injury entry alone would not have established that appearance, but the recorded game does. Dewford, Eterna’s wild-card opponent, has no current positive-week injury entry after scoring thirty-five at Rustboro."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "The byes offer time, with no guaranteed return"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mt. Silver has new absences for Vibrava, five weeks, and Medicham, four. Tic Thorpe remains out three, Josh Alakazam four, Tony Gyarzalez five, Ariados ten and Ninji Asomugha one. Crem Ftzpatrik threw for 160 yards in the finale and Garshawn Lynch rushed for eighty-eight. The first seed removes one game from the championship route, but it does not make every injured player available for the next one."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mossdeep’s Poury Holt remains out six weeks. Shawn Mareman rushed for 153 yards and caught a touchdown in the 27–0 finale, useful evidence of another contributor during Michael Dorrill’s confirmed rest-and-development plan. Mareman’s own new entry has zero remaining weeks; it does not establish an additional absence. The bye and the intentional starter rest should be considered alongside the current availability report, without assuming a playoff lineup."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Other wild-card absences"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Lavender’s Mr. Clanky remains out five weeks before Vermilion visits. Moth Ball’s 248 passing yards and late division-winning drive provide direct evidence of the available quarterback’s work. Vermilion has Drakloak out nine weeks, Gabite one, Exploud two and Delcatty two. Drakloak’s 755 receiving yards make that continuing absence particularly consequential against the Wails."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Petalburg’s Oinkologne remains out two weeks after a 957-yard rushing season. Rustboro’s Milotic is out four. Hearthome has Dodrio out two and Mr. Mime six before the trip to Sunyshore. All durations below are reported recovery counters, not medical diagnoses or guaranteed return dates. A designation reaching zero does not establish activation, a start or game participation."
        },
